he cycle-31 retrospective end marker"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TfGmZmJoPZWKFL5HDQwSF1","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"G:/Codes/LabVIEW_Codes/MinLab/zz_LabView VI/AAA_UNIST/2. Tracking/V6_ParallelLoop\"; until tail -n +172 tools/bench/retro.log | grep -q \"BGRUN\"; do sleep 15; done; tail -3 tools/bench/retro.log","timeout":600000,"description":"Wait for the cycle-31 retrospective end marker"}},{"tool_name":"PowerShell","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CWCwPZww9rox18j8eBT7VY","tool_input":{"command":"(Get-Content \"STATUS.md\" | Measure-Object -Line).Lines","description":"Count STATUS.md lines"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":6,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":6,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":6,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"log-reader":1,"material":5}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":28,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle closed. STATUS is 116 lines (L3 wants ≤110 — six over, and further cutting would delete facts the next cold start needs), machine keys intact, no `STOP` marker, lock released.\n\n**What this cycle did — D0 is delivered.**\n\nThe prior-art review stopped the planned build before it started, and it was right: `drive_original_copy_v3.py` had already executed every clause of D0's done-when on 2026-09-17. So `build_d0_harness_v0.py` was abandoned and never created, and the work became a retarget onto the 4.5 copy instead. That decision cost one dispatch and saved a duplicate harness.\n\nThe first attempt failed — the done button was never hit. I proposed the picking loop was starved of camera frames, because three readings agreed. The peer refuted it: two of those three (`current image number`, the stop Booleans) are **stage-4** signals read inside the frame-loop body, so they were never evidence about the picking stage at all, and the screenshot showed the diagram drawing bead markers while it ran. The real fault was that `(1114,915)` had been inherited from a **different copy** of the VI; the button sits at `(1177,862)`. Click delivery was proven — the pixel was wrong. Locating every click on the live panel turned 13/3 into **39/1**, both legs: picks → done → three bandpass panels → save dialog → experiment loop with frames advancing 8326→10856 → own-control stop in 1.0 s → 285 kB trace file, twice. Original md5 unchanged throughout.\n\nTwo things the user should see, both in STATUS's `FOR THE USER` section: **the VI moved the PI magnet 0 → 30.000 mm under its own control**, inside the 0–39 envelope with the limits holding — Pre-decided 4's assumption is now measured rather than assumed; and the harness **records** all 60 panel controls but **sets** none, which narrows Pre-decided 3 deliberately (inventing parameter values would be a computation change under rule 1a).\n\nThe retrospective named one fault, `inference-over-measurement | loss_min=42 | loss_usd=3.28`, and it is mine — I inherited both the click point and the TMX parse instead of measuring either.\n\nI saved the user's new standing rule — every GUI action is capture → locate → act → capture → confirm, and derived or remembered coordinates are never clicked blind — since it is what fixed this cycle and will apply to every future GUI step. It is also now `docs/cycle27-plan.md` Pre-decided 9. One correction for the record: the user's proposed cause (front panel not maximised) was not what the machine showed — the panel rect measured identical, delta (0,0), three separate times; their remedy was right for a different reason.\n\n`NEXT` opens D1: first the `tmx_from` silent-false-green on motor-limit checks (OPEN 55 — it can pass by reading back the value it just wrote, and the rig is assembled), then N1, the fixture comparison that gates every D1 build.","ttft_ms":231